# The protected set (design 01, section 4).
# One "account class" pair per line; an optional "# reason" after it.
# Classes and what Labyrinth may do to each:
#   official    never changed without the White Team's permission; logons alerted on
#   scoring     never touched by automation
#   employee    used by simulated employees; never touched by automation, keeps password login
#   operator    never locked or removed
#   breakglass  never locked or removed; password rotated only in design 05's order;
#               unregistered SSH keys are still removed
#   service     never touched until the dependency map is known
#   builtin     never touched
# An empty file stops every run. Placeholder names only.

whiteteam        official    # official account named in the event packet
scoring_user1    scoring     # account the scoring engine logs in with
employee1        employee    # account a simulated employee logs in with
operator1        operator    # named team operator
root             breakglass  # existing admin account; rotated password kept in the offline record
svc_webapp       service     # service account a scored service depends on
